 "trap_class": "modified residue dropped",
 "intent": "Write the amino-acid sequence of chain A of the X-ray model xray_model.pdb as one FASTA record (header >chain_A) to chain_A.fasta.",
 "silent_error": "PPBuilder.build_peptides(..., aa_only=1) is the default and means 'the residue needs to be a standard amino acid' (Biopython API docs). Selenomethionine (MSE, written as HETATM in crystal structures) is not standard, so every MSE residue is left out and the chain is cut into pieces around it; joining the pieces gives a 36-residue sequence without the four methionines, including the N-terminal one, instead of the true 40-residue sequence. The FASTA looks like an ordinary protein sequence. Exit status 0, empty stderr.",
 "files": {
  "chain_fasta.py": "import sys\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser, PPBuilder\n\nstructure = PDBParser().get_structure('s', sys.argv[1])\nchain = structure[0]['A']\nseq = ''.join(str(pp.get_sequence()) for pp in PPBuilder().build_peptides(chain))\nprint('>chain_A')\nprint(seq)\n",
